[38;5;231m⏺[39m Done — took the CA-pinning option (the one I recommended), so production keeps full certificate validation.

  [38;5;153mclient.py[39m:
  - Added [38;5;153mVERIFY: str | bool = os.environ.get("REPORTS_CA_BUNDLE") or True[39m — a path when the env var is set, otherwise
    normal system-trust verification.
  - Both [38;5;153mrequests.get[39m calls now pass [38;5;153mverify=VERIFY[39m.

  To run the staging sync, point it at the self-signed cert:

  REPORTS_CA_BUNDLE=/path/to/staging-ca.pem python scripts/sync_staging.py

  If staging's cert is self-signed rather than issued by a local CA, the cert file itself works as the bundle.
  [38;5;153mscripts/export_prod.py[39m is untouched and unaffected — with the env var unset it verifies exactly as before.

  Checks: [38;5;153mruff check client.py[39m passes. [38;5;153mmypy[39m only reports missing [38;5;153mtypes-requests[39m stubs (pre-existing, unrelated to this
  change); I didn't install packages. No test suite exists in the repo, so nothing was run beyond a syntax/parse check —
  I did not make a live request against either host.

